---
import LegalPage from "../components/LegalPage.astro";
import { CONTACT_EMAILS, MARKETING_SITE_URL } from "../lib/site";

const sections = [
  ["scope", "Scope"],
  ["source", "Open-source software"],
  ["responsibilities", "Your responsibilities"],
  ["third-parties", "Third-party services"],
  ["availability", "Availability and changes"],
  ["disclaimers", "Disclaimers"],
  ["liability", "Limitation of liability"],
  ["law", "Governing law"],
  ["contact", "Contact"],
] as const;
---

<LegalPage
  title="Terms of Use — Not Codex"
  description="Terms for the Not Codex website and public source repository."
  heading="Not Codex Terms of Use"
  lede="These terms cover the public Not Codex website and source repository. They do not describe a hosted application, paid plan, or account service."
  effectiveDate="2026-07-21"
  lastUpdated="2026-07-21"
  sections={sections}
>
  <section id="scope">
    <p class="section-number">01</p><h2>Scope</h2>
    <p>These terms apply when you visit <a href={MARKETING_SITE_URL}>{MARKETING_SITE_URL}</a> (the “Site”) or interact with the public Not Codex source repository. The Site is operated by Yossi Elkrief under the MaTrixy and BPro names (“we,” “us,” or “our”).</p>
    <p><strong>Not Codex is independent and is not affiliated with, sponsored by, or endorsed by OpenAI, T3 Tools Inc., or the T3 Code project. Codex is a product and brand of OpenAI.</strong></p>
  </section>
  <section id="source">
    <p class="section-number">02</p><h2>Open-source software</h2>
    <p>The Not Codex source code is offered under the licenses and notices contained in its repository. Those license terms—not these Site terms—govern your use, copying, modification, and distribution of the software. The project’s names, logos, and visual identity are addressed separately in the repository’s trademark policy.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="responsibilities">
    <p class="section-number">03</p><h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
    <p>Not Codex can direct coding agents that execute commands and modify files. You are responsible for evaluating the source, securing your devices and credentials, backing up your work, reviewing agent actions, and complying with laws and third-party terms. Do not use the Site or project to harm others, compromise systems, or infringe rights.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="third-parties">
    <p class="section-number">04</p><h2>Third-party services</h2>
    <p>The Site and repository may link to GitHub, coding-agent providers, package registries, and other third parties. We do not operate those services and their own terms and privacy practices apply. A link or interoperability statement does not imply endorsement.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="availability">
    <p class="section-number">05</p><h2>Availability and changes</h2>
    <p>This is an early work in progress. We may change or discontinue Site content and project features without notice. References to future packages, hosted access, integrations, or releases are plans rather than commitments.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="disclaimers">
    <p class="section-number">06</p><h2>Disclaimers</h2>
    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, the Site and project materials are provided “as is” and “as available,” without warranties of any kind. Nothing on the Site is legal, security, or professional advice.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="liability">
    <p class="section-number">07</p><h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, we will not be liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or loss of data, profits, goodwill, or business opportunity arising from the Site or project materials. Rights that cannot lawfully be limited remain unaffected.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="law">
    <p class="section-number">08</p><h2>Governing law</h2>
    <p>These Site terms are governed by the laws of Israel, without regard to conflict-of-law principles. Subject to mandatory consumer law, disputes relating to these terms are subject to the competent courts in Israel.</p>
  </section>
  <section id="contact">
    <p class="section-number">09</p><h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>Legal questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAILS.legal}`}>{CONTACT_EMAILS.legal}</a>. Support questions: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAILS.support}`}>{CONTACT_EMAILS.support}</a>.</p>
  </section>
</LegalPage>
